  "notes": "Herdr fork preview (wwelder/herdr): every worker folds under its caller and stays quiet\n\nSource: f4cdeb3c533ac0368c5562bec0ef6e9d6ea9c4cc.\n\n- A workspace's lowest-numbered agent pane is its caller. Every other agent in that workspace, and every `codex exec` run, is a subagent. One predicate sets `agent.list`'s `subagent` flag, and the TUI panel folds subagents under their caller.\n- Subagents send no toast, sound, push or Gram alert.\n- This replaces the rule that made a Codex agent without a session a subagent, which also silenced an interactive Codex before it reported its session.\n- Includes the host APM change from 2026-11-06-c55ccbf20a43: the APM counts every user on the machine.\n\nAll five assets were built by the manual Build artifacts workflow (run 42328536767).\n\nUpdate with `herdr update` on the preview channel.",
